<title>USA: FGIC qualifies six issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>FGIC qualifies six issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Guaranty Insurance Co. said it has qualified for bond insurance the following six municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Lafayette Elem SD, Calif., $12.3 million General obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Pinckney Community Schools, Mich., $73 million school building bonds.</p>
<p>--Apex, N.C., $3 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Roswell Independent School District, N.M., $5 million school building bonds.</p>
<p>--Lakeway, Texas, $1.6 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Middletown, N.J., $78.4 million.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
</text>
